The {{nihongo|'''Shitayanagi Line'''|下柳線|Shitayanagi-sen}} is a subway line in [[Okami|Okami (大紙)]], [[Okaiken]], operated by [[Okami Metro]]. It serves as a vital western distributor, running parallel to the [[Miyoshi Line]] through the city's western commercial districts before curving south towards the bay area. On system maps, the line is color-coded canary yellow ({{Okami Metro color|S}}), and its stations use the prefix "S".

The Shitayanagi Line is known as the "Connector Line" because it intersects with almost every other east-west line in the network (Asahi, Chūō, Nagata, Tozai) without passing through the congested [[Okami Central Station]]. This makes it a popular bypass route for savvy commuters avoiding the central hub.



==History==
Planned in the 1970s to develop the western side of the Loop Line, the Shitayanagi Line was constructed in phases. The northern section between [[Noda-Hanshin Station|Noda-Hanshin]] and [[Sakuragawa Station|Sakuragawa]] opened on May 25, 1975.

The line was extended south to [[Suminoe-Koen Station|Suminoe-Koen]] in 1982 to serve the Okami Bay Area and the boat racing stadium. Unlike the 10-car Miyoshi Line trains, the Shitayanagi Line utilizes shorter 6-car trainsets, reflecting its role as a distributor rather than a primary artery.

